From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix: return device removal from Present
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: after device removal Present kept returning S_OK while nothing
rendered, so one slow dispatch left a permanently black game that still
"presents" (cursor visible, frame counter running) (V3).

Root cause: dxgi_vk_swap_chain_Present never checked the device's removed
reason; vkd3d only reported removal through submits and fences.

Fix: once the device is removed, Present returns the removed reason
(DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED), as DXGI does, before doing any work.

Verified by: hang probe with MVK_CONFIG_RESUME_LOST_DEVICE=0: Present returns
0x887a0005 (N§27); device_removed_reason and fence-wait robustness tests
rechecked after the step-6 sweep (N§27e).

Off switch: none.
---
 libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
index 2c6e9c7..2a13048 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1129,6 +1129,14 @@ static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE dxgi_vk_swap_chain_Present(IDXGIVkSwapChain2 *i
             iface, SyncInterval, PresentFlags, pPresentParameters);
     (void)pPresentParameters;
 
+    /* Like DXGI: once the device is removed, Present fails instead of silently presenting nothing,
+     * so the application notices (and can query GetDeviceRemovedReason / recreate the device). */
+    {
+        HRESULT removed = d3d12_device_removed_reason(chain->queue->device);
+        if (FAILED(removed))
+            return removed;
+    }
+
     if (dxgi_vk_swap_chain_present_is_occluded(chain, PresentFlags))
         return DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED;
     if (PresentFlags & DXGI_PRESENT_TEST)
